FILE: vUX-spaEngine.js
FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON
The delegated SPA-link click handler discarded its handle and the popstate handler was an
anonymous closure, so an engine could never be shut down: its links kept intercepting
clicks and its popstate handler kept rewriting the page. The popstate handler is now held
in an instance-scope variable (assigned rather than reindented, to keep the diff to the
binding itself), the click handle is stored, and the cache builder's setTimeout id is kept
so a pending build can be cancelled.

destroy() detaches both listeners, cancels the cache builder and drops the cached page
sections. Browser history is deliberately not unwound: the entries this engine pushed are
the user's navigation record, not the engine's private state.

